###### _Prevention_ 

Hydrogen blistering can basically be prevented by means of the following measures: 

- process modifications to ensure that either the formation of the previously mentioned acid components is suppressed very largely if not entirely, or that those components are removed (e.g., washed out in a scrubber at an early stage); 

- dosing of corrosion inhibitors to the medium; 

###### _Prevention_ 

Hydride formation can be minimized by building a thick protective oxide film by means of anodizing or thermooxidative treatments. Pickling in a mixture of nitric acid and hydrogen, fluoride is applied to remove iron contamination. Cathodic coupling (with consequent H2 formation) with other metals must of course be avoided. 

